```{r}
#| label: fig-trajectory
#| fig-cap: "Environmental Index trajectory of the evaluated locations across years"
#| warning: false
#| message: false

library(tidyverse)
library(ggplot2)
library(ggrepel)

trajectory_index <- df_filter %>%
  group_by(env, loc, YEAR, RAINFED) %>% 
  summarise(GY_mean = mean(GY, na.rm = TRUE), .groups = "drop") %>%
  mutate(index = GY_mean - mean(df_filter$GY, na.rm = TRUE)) %>%
  group_by(loc) %>%
  mutate(total_years = n_distinct(YEAR)) %>%
  ungroup()

ggplot(trajectory_index, aes(x = factor(YEAR), y = index, group = loc)) +
  geom_line(data = subset(trajectory_index, total_years > 1), 
            aes(colour = loc), linewidth = 1, alpha = 0.8) +
  geom_hline(yintercept = 0, linetype = "dashed", linewidth = 0.8, colour = "grey40") +
  
  geom_point(data = subset(trajectory_index, total_years > 1),
             aes(shape = as.factor(RAINFED)), colour = "black", size = 4, stroke = 1.2) +
  geom_point(data = subset(trajectory_index, total_years == 1),
             aes(shape = as.factor(RAINFED)), colour = "firebrick", size = 4, stroke = 1.2) +
  
  ggrepel::geom_text_repel(aes(label = env), colour = "grey50", size = 3, 
                           nudge_x = 0.2,       
                           direction = "y",    
                           segment.color = "grey80") + 
  
  scale_colour_viridis_d(option = "turbo", name = "Location Code") +
  scale_shape_manual(values = c(16, 15, 8), name = "Water Regime") + 
  
  labs(x = "Year", 
       y = "Environmental Index",
       title = "Location Trajectory and Water Regime Impact",
       subtitle = "") +
  
  theme_minimal(base_size = 14) +
  theme(legend.position = "right",
        panel.grid.minor = element_blank())

```
The environmental index exhibited a substantial amplitude, ranging from approximately -2,000 kg/ha to +2,300 kg/ha, evidencing a strong environmental effect on grain yield across the testing network. The most severe stress conditions were recorded in E0107 (2019, Rainfed), which presented the lowest index, whereas E0279 (2023) stood out completely from the rest as the most favorable environment of the entire network, representing a condition of high yield potential. It is also noteworthy that the majority of the evaluated environments were concentrated in the 2023 season.

Analyzing the impact of water regimes over the years reveals a distinct temporal pattern. In 2019 and 2020, all trials within the network were conducted under rainfed conditions. Remarkably, even without supplementary water, several of these early rainfed environments (such as E0106, E0176, E0171, E0172, and E0169) managed to achieve positive environmental indices. However, a clear shift occurred from 2021 onwards: no rainfed trial managed to reach a positive index. During this later period, positive yield performances became exclusively associated with irrigated or supplementary water regimes.

From a location-specific perspective, L074 is uniquely positioned as the only location comprising trials across all evaluated years, having started with rainfed conditions in its first two seasons. Location L118 stands out as highly interesting, almost consistently maintaining excellent positive indices, with only a minor decrease observed in 2021. Conversely, locations L078 and L075 were chronically unfavorable, consistently recording negative indices across all their trials. Finally, as shown in @fig-trajectory, the frequent crossovers between the location lines over the years indicate that environmental rankings shift dynamically between seasons, which strongly anticipates the presence of a relevant Genotype × Environment (G×E) interaction in the network.


